],"metadata":{"id":"XGiHE83QYuXI"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This function show the plot and numbers related to our simulations."],"metadata":{"id":"aKasFhWGXHFe"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def show_results(results):\n","  plt.hist(results, label=f'N = {N}')\n","  plt.title(f'Distribution of Earnings for N = {N}')\n","  plt.xlabel('Earnings')\n","  plt.ylabel('Density')\n","  plt.legend()\n","  plt.show()\n","\n","  mean = sum(results) / len(results)\n","  std_dev = (sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in results) / len(results)) ** 0.5\n","  print(f'For N = {N}: Mean = {mean:.2f}, Standard Deviation = {std_dev:.2f}')"],"metadata":{"id":"Ch0vftaoXIHd"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["At last we use these functions to run Monte Carlo simulation for given rounds and show results."],"metadata":{"id":"VK6cJFITXV69"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["rounds = [10, 25, 100, 1000]\n","for N in rounds:\n","  earnings = monte_carlo_simulation_sum(N)\n","  show_results(earnings)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"86O3wPwNOvmT","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983227732,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":90291,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"2b449504-41a0-43f6-a21d-3c4f67cb4821"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 10: Mean = -0.53, Standard Deviation = 3.16\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 25: Mean = -1.33, Standard Deviation = 5.00\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 100: Mean = -5.32, Standard Deviation = 9.98\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 1000: Mean = -52.60, Standard Deviation = 31.67\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["As you can see in our results, the plot is similar to normal distribution.\n","\n","The avearage is increasing with $N$ in same scale, the ratio is approximately -5.2% of $N$.\n","\n","Also the standard deviation is increasing by increasing $N$."],"metadata":{"id":"Jd7goqqwc6ZP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["###<font color='skyblue'>3.  Monte Carlo Simulation for $\\frac{S_N}{N}$</font>\n"],"metadata":{"id":"acuFeHn3UnrZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["In this part we define another Monte Carlo simulation function that give average of results for $N$ instead of summation of them."],"metadata":{"id":"CsM2skc0egwC"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def monte_carlo_simulation_avg(N, simulations=100000):\n","    results = [roulette_sim(N) / N for _ in range(simulations)]\n","    return results"],"metadata":{"id":"-SQpAU2EV2AS"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["We repeat last time for this new simulation function and plot the results."],"metadata":{"id":"EtKHwIUcfei_"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["rounds = [10, 25, 100, 1000]\n","for N in rounds:\n","  earnings = monte_carlo_simulation_avg(N)\n","  show_results(earnings)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"e9YMrcjnfsU0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983298263,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":70537,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"67672de8-24cd-42c2-80d0-a84641d6602f"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 10: Mean = -0.05, Standard Deviation = 0.32\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 25: Mean = -0.05, Standard Deviation = 0.20\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 100: Mean = -0.05, Standard Deviation = 0.10\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["For N = 1000: Mean = -0.05, Standard Deviation = 0.03\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The plots still seem to be similar to normal distribution specially as $N$ increase, but unlike last part here the mean is almost the same for all of them and the standard deviation is decreasing."],"metadata":{"id":"Zv8AeGT9fw5w"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["###<font color='skyblue'>4.  Theoretical Calculation</font>\n"],"metadata":{"id":"s5FWvREbhIpX"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["According to given distribution for winning the expected value and standard deviation will be as below:\n","\n","(It's similar to binomial distribution formulas but with difference that the values are 1 and -1, instead of 1 and 0.)\n","\n","$$\\mu_N =N( \\frac{9}{19} - \\frac{10}{19})= -\\frac{N}{19} ≃ -0.0526N$$\n","\n","$$\\sigma_N =2\\sqrt{ N. \\frac{9}{19} . \\frac{10}{19}}\\simeq \\sqrt N$$\n","We show theoretical values with $_t$ and the Monte Carlo results with $_{mc}$.\n","* $N=10 : \\mu_{t} = -0.526, \\mu_{mc}= -0.52 , σ_t=3.16 , σ_{mc}=3.16$\n","* $N=25 : \\mu_{t} = -1.315, \\mu_{mc}= -1.30 , σ_t=5 , σ_{mc}=4.98$\n","* $N=100 : \\mu_{t} = -5.26, \\mu_{mc}= -5.25 , σ_t=10 , σ_{mc}=9.93$\n","* $N=1000 : \\mu_{t} = -52.6, \\mu_{mc}= -52.57 , σ_t=31.6 , σ_{mc}=31.54$\n","\n","As you can see the results are pretty close in theoretical and Monte Carlo methods and get closer with increase of $N$."],"metadata":{"id":"3COEzJDvk-px"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def theoretical_values(N):\n","    P = 9 / 19\n","    expected_value = N * (P - (1 - P))\n","    standard_error = 2 * (N * P * (1 - P)) ** 0.5\n","    return expected_value, standard_error"],"metadata":{"id":"xiodLhlYA5_u"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["###<font color='skyblue'>5. Calculating Probability of Casino Losing Money</font>\n"],"metadata":{"id":"cRt2je2_8yrj"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["By using CLT we assume that the distribution of $S_N$ is normal and calculate this probability with a normal distribution that we make with our theoretical mean and std.\n","\n","Using the function we defined in last part to calculate theoretical values for $N$; we define a function that calculate the probability of casino loss ($S_N$>0) in below function"],"metadata":{"id":"kDEtR42s-W4F"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def probability_of_loss(N):\n","    expected_value, standard_error = theoretical_values(N)\n","    prob = 1-norm.cdf(0, loc=expected_value, scale=standard_error)\n","    return prob"],"metadata":{"id":"QoSG2tRPD8we"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["We test our function in below and as you can see it's working pretty well since the probability is almost same as Monte Carlo approximation."],"metadata":{"id":"VRuSsLeHEn_b"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["N = 25\n","simulated_earnings = monte_carlo_simulation_sum(N)\n","casino_loss_probability = sum(1 for s in simulated_earnings if s > 0) / len(simulated_earnings)\n","clt_probability = probability_of_loss(N)\n","\n","print(f'Simulated Probability of Loss: {casino_loss_probability:.4f}')\n","print(f'CLT Approximation: {clt_probability:.4f}')\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"NzMKSu6r9rs6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983298660,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":410,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"d50a4b93-4b98-4802-8703-596e2fa29ad6"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Simulated Probability of Loss: 0.3933\n","CLT Approximation: 0.3961\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["###<font color='skyblue'>6. Effect of $N$ in Probability of Casino Losing Money</font>"],"metadata":{"id":"9DbD3XZ1FGQb"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["As $N$ increases, the probability of the casino losing money decreases due to the law of large numbers, so casino encourage players to continue betting since it means increasing of $N$."],"metadata":{"id":"Y8TE2FUAFefR"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["rounds = range(25, 1000)\n","loss_probabilities = [probability_of_loss(N) for N in rounds]\n","\n","plt.plot(rounds, loss_probabilities)\n","plt.title('Probability of Casino Losing Money vs. N')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Rounds (N)')\n","plt.ylabel('Probability of Casino Losing Money')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"BuMT5TPyFguM","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983299381,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":729,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"9b310963-1011-4d14-891f-1c1774406d6f"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2ZdCahFSIA6G"},"source":["## <font color='orange'>**Election Prediction**</font>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"jzHnnEbMIA6J"},"source":["### <font color='skyblue'>1. Confidence Interval Calcuation</font>\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"pSLWx0zJIA6L"},"source":["A needed K\\% confidence interval for p has the general form:\n","\n","$$\n","\\hat{p} \\pm z_{\\alpha/2} \\cdot \\text{SE}(\\hat{p}),\n","$$\n","\n","where $z_{\\alpha/2}$ is the critical value from the standard normal distribution (for K\\% it is $\\frac{(1-K)}{2}$ so for 95\\% confidence it is 0.025, and $z_{0.025} \\approx 1.96$) and $\\text{SE}(\\hat{p})$ is the standard error of $\\hat{p}$.\n","\n","The standard error is estimated by:\n","\n","$$\n","\\text{SE}(\\hat{p}) \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{\\hat{p}(1-\\hat{p})}{N}}.\n","$$\n","\n","Therefore, the 95\\% CI for $p$ is:\n","\n","$$\n","\\hat{p} \\;\\pm\\; 1.96 \\,\\sqrt{\\frac{\\hat{p}(1-\\hat{p})}{N}}.\n","$$\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"OyHovGuIIA6L"},"source":["### <font color='skyblue'>2. Monte Carlo Simulation</font>\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"6Iav-s7mIA6M","outputId":"cc355a5e-87c1-4123-dffe-6d82132c3aca","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983299687,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":314,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["0.93092\n"]}],"source":["import numpy as np\n","\n","p = 0.47\n","NUM_ITER = 100000\n","N = 30\n","num_true = 0\n","\n","for _ in range(NUM_ITER):\n","\n","    dist = np.random.binomial(n=N, p=p)\n","\n","    p_hat = dist / N\n","\n","    margin = 1.96 * np.sqrt(p_hat * (1 - p_hat) / N)\n","\n","    if (p >= p_hat - margin) and (p <= p_hat + margin):\n","        num_true += 1\n","\n","print(num_true / NUM_ITER)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"R3wMnCHaIA6N"},"source":["We see 0.93 in our result and it is natural. The classic Wald interval\n","\n","$$\n","\\hat{p} \\pm 1.96 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\hat{p}(1-\\hat{p})}{N}}\n","$$\n","\n","is known to produce a coverage probability below 95\\% when the sample size is small (here, $N=30$) or when $p$ is not close to 0.5 (which is not the case here). This under-coverage happens because the standard error is estimated using $\\hat{p}$, and the normal approximation doesn’t hold perfectly in small samples."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1yz5PlFmIA6O"},"source":["### <font color='skyblue'>3. Loading Election Dataset</font>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["First we download datasets needed for this project:"],"metadata":{"id":"y-Vo4ejIQTmX"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import os\n","\n","if not os.path.exists(\"dataset_flag\"):\n","  !gdown 1GlPmHWefIm8c_76dLYzmm8_AyB7Cdhog\n","  !gdown 1SUIAu9NbigUTLbPzW3KPtAvr5xHVDI9Y\n","  !touch dataset_flag"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"Dv48q-RvejE3","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983320164,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":20479,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"b5435144-a28a-4884-de94-1d9268276b88"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Downloading...\n","From: https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1GlPmHWefIm8c_76dLYzmm8_AyB7Cdhog\n","To: /content/drug_safety.csv\n","100% 563k/563k [00:00<00:00, 69.5MB/s]\n","Downloading...\n","From: https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1SUIAu9NbigUTLbPzW3KPtAvr5xHVDI9Y\n","To: /content/2016-general-election-trump-vs-clinton.csv\n","100% 557k/557k [00:00<00:00, 89.5MB/s]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Here we load the election dataset:"],"metadata":{"id":"7e-IQw7hQY47"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"EpLE7gm4IA6P","outputId":"23e8295d-48b4-4adc-e0e7-f691791cc50a","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":223},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983320930,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":775,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["False\n"]},{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["   Trump  Clinton          Pollster  Start Date  Number of Observations  \\\n","0   41.0     45.0     Insights We