\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Candidate\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"Clinton\",\n          \"Trump\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Estimated Proportion\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.035558789765176076,\n        \"min\": 0.40583307701304167,\n        \"max\": 0.4561207997605273,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.4561207997605273,\n          0.40583307701304167\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Total Candidate Votes\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 69017,\n        \"min\": 787694,\n        \"max\": 885299,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          885299,\n          787694\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Estimated CI\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"object\",\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Two Class Proportion\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.04125370361843289,\n        \"min\": 0.47082922642234604,\n        \"max\": 0.5291707735776539,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.5291707735776539,\n          0.47082922642234604\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":19}],"source":["results[\"Two Class Proportion\"] = results[\"Estimated Proportion\"] * (1 / results[\"Estimated Proportion\"].sum())\n","\n","results"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"xPzWwq7zIA6V"},"source":["Now with these updated proportions, we calculate our d-estimation. Note that for this part, since we are considering only Trump and Clinton, the total votes used will be the sum of votes for these two candidates; votes for other candidates are excluded."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"rHr4v6aGIA6V","outputId":"c24386d1-e3f0-423c-fe46-d8dc75d4951e","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983322950,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":51,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["[0.05683, 0.05985]"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":20}],"source":["def calculate_d_interval(p_hat, N):\n","    margin = 1.96 * 2 * np.sqrt(p_hat * (1 - p_hat) / N)\n","    d = 2 * p_hat - 1\n","    return [round(d - margin,5), round(d + margin,5)]\n","\n","total_two_class_votes = results[\"Total Candidate Votes\"].sum()\n","\n","clinton_two_class_proportion = results.loc[results[\"Candidate\"] == \"Clinton\", \"Two Class Proportion\"].iloc[0]\n","\n","Estimated_D_CI = calculate_d_interval(clinton_two_class_proportion, total_two_class_votes)\n","\n","Estimated_D_CI"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"DJAlcKFtIA6W"},"source":["**Hypothesis testing**\n","\n","What we want to test:\n","$$\n","H_0: d = 0 \\quad\\text{vs.}\\quad H_a: d \\neq 0\n","$$  \n","is equivalent to testing whether  \n","$$\n","p = 0.5\n","$$  \n","since $d = 0$ if and only if $p = 0.5$.\n","\n","If we denote $\\hat{p}$ as the estimated proportion (here, for Clinton’s share in the two-class race), then the standard error for $\\hat{p}$ under the null (with $p = 0.5$) is\n","$$\n","SE_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{0.5(1-0.5)}{N}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{0.25}{N}} = \\frac{0.5}{\\sqrt{N}},\n","$$\n","where $N$ is the total number of votes in the two-class race (votes for Trump and Clinton).\n","\n","Thus, the test statistic is\n","$$\n","z = \\frac{\\hat{p} - 0.5}{SE_0} = \\frac{\\hat{p} - 0.5}{0.5/\\sqrt{N}} = 2\\sqrt{N} (\\hat{p} - 0.5).\n","$$\n","\n","Once $z$ is computed, the two-sided $p$-value is given by\n","$$\n","p\\text{-value} = 2\\Pr(Z > |z|),\n","$$\n","where $Z$ follows the standard normal distribution:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"ZL4LcSstIA6W","outputId":"b44da4b9-46f6-4065-a6d3-e10a93dfb4a9","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983322951,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":45,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["clinton_two_class_proportion: 0.5291707735776539\n","z: 75.46142531183591\n","p_value: 0.0\n"]}],"source":["from scipy.stats import norm\n","\n","z = 2 * np.sqrt(total_two_class_votes) * (clinton_two_class_proportion - 0.5)\n","\n","p_value = 2 * (1 - norm.cdf(np.abs(z)))\n","\n","print(\"clinton_two_class_proportion:\",clinton_two_class_proportion)\n","print(\"z:\",z)\n","print(\"p_value:\",p_value)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"prBDn451IA6W"},"source":["And therefor we reject H_0, which makes sense based on the value of `clinton two class proportion` (approx. 0.53) and the very high value of z (75.46)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## <font color='orange'>**Drug Safety Test**</font>\n"],"metadata":{"id":"yRWcj2XddwYT"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The dataset comes from a randomized controlled drug trial conducted by a medical group and shared by Vanderbilt University Department of Biostatistics. The study evaluates drug safety by comparing a Drug and Placebo group while tracking adverse effects, vital signs, and lab measures.\n","\n","Columns Explanation:\n","* age: Age of the participant\n","* sex: Gender of the participant (male or female).\n","* trx: Treatment group:\n","* \"Drug\" → Received the actual drug.\n","* \"Placebo\" → Received a placebo (control group).\n","* week: Week number in the