1717c5b378b"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["T-test result for wbc:\n","t-statistic: -0.6596884009910975, p-value: 0.5094775322580585\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for rbc:\n","t-statistic: 1.8239231444207347, p-value: 0.06821193346979416\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for num_effects:\n","t-statistic: 0.6982668655753146, p-value: 0.48503538645811195\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for adverse_effects:\n","t-statistic: 0.6047130244978415, p-value: 0.54539110892564\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["As we see, we failed to reject the null hypothesis and there was no significant different between each pair."],"metadata":{"id":"Liu3Uis6pbTs"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**4. Perform t-tests for each metric, use p-value = 0.1**"],"metadata":{"id":"1GDDQz09pqq-"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["metrics = ['wbc', 'rbc', 'num_effects', 'adverse_effects']\n","\n","for metric in metrics:\n","    perform_ttest(metric, alternative='two-sided', equal_var=False, significance_level=0.1)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"0EDTNZuUprzD","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1741983322953,"user_tz":-210,"elapsed":20,"user":{"displayName":"Aidin Kazemi","userId":"10743926351232888178"}},"outputId":"99489e8a-2303-4edf-d951-68294d655fef"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["T-test result for wbc:\n","t-statistic: -0.6596884009910975, p-value: 0.5094775322580585\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for rbc:\n","t-statistic: 1.8239231444207347, p-value: 0.06821193346979416\n","Reject the null hypothesis: Significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for num_effects:\n","t-statistic: 0.6982668655753146, p-value: 0.48503538645811195\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n","T-test result for adverse_effects:\n","t-statistic: 0.6047130244978415, p-value: 0.54539110892564\n","Fail to reject the null hypothesis: No significant difference.\n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["When we increased significance level to 0.1, red blood cell count t-test reject the null hypothesis and has significance diference"],"metadata":{"id":"CJS4wytRp9xv"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Significance level meaning:**\n","\n","For each test, if the p-value is less than significance_level, we will reject the null hypothesis, indicating a significant difference.\n","\n","If the p-value is greater than significance_level, you will fail to reject the null hypothesis.\n","\n","**Alternative argument**\n","\n","The alternative argument in the scipy function specifies the direction of the alternative hypothesis in the t-test. It defines whether we are testing for a two-sided or one-sided difference between the two groups being compared.\n","\n","For each metric, we use 'two-sided', which tests for any significant difference between the Drug and Placebo groups in either direction.\n","\n","**equal_var argument**\n","\n","We set equal_var=False as we generally don't assume equal variances between the Drug and Placebo groups unless there's prior knowledge suggesting otherwise."],"metadata":{"id":"1LDnZPMnqg4f"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##<font color='orange'>**Bonus Question**</font>\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"fnWK5W9mHQUA"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The answer is :\n","\n","**2. To estimate the true average pressure of the pipeline and give ourselves some room for error in the estimate.**\n","\n","A 95% confidence interval for $\\mu$ is constructed to estimate the true average (mean) of the population (in this case, the true average pressure of the pipeline). This interval provides a range of values that we are 95% confident contains the true average $\\mu$, accounting for the variability introduced by the random error ($ϵ_i$) in the model."],"metadata":{"id":"JKqhU49QHbwu"}}]}